sec.p:
To investigate the effect of inflammation on drug exposure, IL-6 levels were used as an inflammation indicator. We digitized data from previously published studies characterizing CYP3A4 activity in relation to IL-6 levels in human hepatocytes [19, 20]. For GFR, we used a healthy volunteer endotoxemia study [12], which described the relationship between GFR and IL-6 levels. The data from these studies were digitized using PlotDigitizer (version 3.1.5) (Fig. S1 in the Supplementary Information). Nonlinear and linear relationships were fitted to describe the relationships between IL-6 and CYP3A4 activity (Eq. 1) and GFR (Eq. 2), respectively. The fitting was performed using the “optim” and “lm” functions in the statistical software R (version 4.2.1).1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
