The total body clearance (CL) was defined as the sum of the hepatic plasma clearance and renal plasma clearance (Eq. 7). The hepatic clearance was exclusively based on the CYP3A4-mediated metabolism and the renal clearance was based on the GFR-mediated elimination of the unbound drug (Eq. 8):7\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
